== step 1: THERE IS NO APPLE REFERENCE, AND THAT IS THE POINT ==
   This payload builds NOTHING on this Mac and compares nothing to it.
   A wall-clock number is a property of ONE box, and the comparison
   that matters is made ON the rented box, in one hour, between our
   FAST arm and the vendor's own library running on the same silicon
   under the same thermal conditions. Carrying an M4 millisecond into
   that table would be comparing two machines and calling it a
   comparison of two libraries.

   What comes home is FSPEED lines. The verdict is
   tools/fast_speed_table.py, run HERE, over the fetched logs.

